{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Shield</b> — Rabbi Moses the Kohen said: the pronominal suffix in גבורהו with the appended heh is plural form, like בהתפללו בעד רעהו. And he did not speak correctly, for פיו is like פיהו, אחיו, אחיהו, שיו, שיהו, and the meaning of רעהו is that he prayed on behalf of each one." "<b>And his might</b> — a generic noun encompassing the might of the mighty." "<b>Like torches</b> — מתלעים: that they wear crimson [scarlet-dyed] garments." "<b>On the day he prepared</b> — הכינו: the chariots, as though fire of bolts of lightning goes forth in their racing. And the word פלדות is foreign; perhaps it is inverted from לפידות." "<b>And the cypresses were envenomed</b> — like רעדו ברושי היער. And Yefet said: they are spears."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:35.420718951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}